sudo nano /etc/apache2/mods-enabled/security2.conf
Make sure the file looks exactly like this. Notice that we uncomment the *.conf line so your custom rules will load, but we leave the OWASP Core Rule Set (*.load) commented out:
<IfModule security2_module>
        # Default Debian modsecurity settings
        SecDataDir /var/cache/modsecurity

        # ENABLED: This allows Apache to read your custom rules folder
        IncludeOptional /etc/modsecurity/*.conf

        # REMAIN COMMENTED OUT: Keeps default OWASP rules disabled
        # IncludeOptional /usr/share/modsecurity-crs/*.load
</IfModule>
